{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_d7cqa4lqezjjxsivszpol3skovkmdsdiy7qulteccl6mccdxxkva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's the summary.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Requirement | Status |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md`: `nm -D` shows 0 missing/undefined non-libc symbols | ✅ symbol diff **empty** (9/9), sizes identical, 0 unresolved (`RTLD_NOW` opens cleanly) |\n| Phase B: every `CONFIGS.md` row passes across randomized inputs | ✅ 70 rows, **0 unchecked** |\n| Phase C: every `ERRORS.md` row has a passing differential test | ✅ 36 rows |\n| Holds under every feature combination | ✅ `run_all.sh` → **ALL FEATURE COMBINATIONS PASSED** (3 feature sets × 2 test profiles × 2 cdylib profiles; 57 result lines, 0 failures) |\n\n## What I found and fixed in the translation\n\n1. **The reference C build has `assert()` LIVE.** The task's cmake command sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so `NDEBUG` is undefined and `__assert_fail` is in `nm -D -u`. The translation had *deliberately dropped* all 10 asserts, so it returned a value where the reference `.so` dies with `SIGABRT`. I translated them behind a `c-asserts` feature (**on by default**); `--no-default-features` reproduces a `-DNDEBUG` build, and the harness picks the matching C library. The harness compares the normalised assert *diagnostics*, so \"the same assert fired\" is checked, not assumed.\n2. **`cp_decode`'s assert shifts by 32** when a tree entry has a zero code length. I confirmed from the reference disassembly that gcc emits a 32-bit variable shift (`shr %cl,%esi`), so the count is taken mod 32 — `wrapping_shr`.\n3. **`unfilter`'s `raw[x] += 0` prologue was folded away.** The add is a no-op but the read-modify-write is not: with a large `bpp` the C library faults there. Now done with `read_volatile`/`write_volatile` (LLVM deletes a plain `x += 0`).\n4. **`[profile.dev]` needed `overflow-checks`/`debug-assertions` off**, otherwise a `cargo build` (dev) artifact turned the C code's UB (writing through a NULL `out`) into a Rust abort where C segfaults.\n\n## The one remaining divergence — and it's proven UB\n\n`cp_dynamic` writes past `uint8_t lens[288+32]`, and gcc places that function's own `int` locals right behind it, so at `n == 364` the code-length loop **zeroes its own counter and the C library spins forever** (I confirmed the hang site by sampling `RIP` from a `SIGALRM` handler: `cp_dynamic+0x1f8`, the `case 18` loop, and mapped every overshoot offset to its frame slot).\n\nRather than assert that classification, the harness proves it: it builds the *same unmodified* `c_src/src/lib.c` a second time with `-fstack-protector-all`, which only moves locals around. Any input whose behaviour differs between two such C builds can only depend on the frame layout. Over **5881 randomized corrupt inputs**: 37 layout-dependent, **0 unexplained**; plus 4000 randomized `unfilter` argument sets with 0 divergences.\n\nI also validated the harness itself with mutation testing (a single-value change to the Average filter, and a `cp_paeth` branch swap, were both caught), and hardened it after finding that per-case `mmap` + concurrent `fork()` let the kernel reuse an address under a waiting parent — that produced *phantom* divergences, so `run()` now uses one serialized, permanently-mapped region and raises a loud `HARNESS ERROR` rather than reporting an incomplete child as a library outcome."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":474693,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":579,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"28b3a684-8905-4a82-aea2-ff9018e78198","uuid":"e00cf4b2-4400-4e2d-b45c-710aa5f04841","timestamp":"2026-08-27T21:38:34.782Z"}
